{"id":37,"text":"A crow found a big piece of cheese. She was very happy. She flew up to a high branch of a tree and sat there. She wanted to eat her cheese in peace.\n\nA hungry fox walked past. He looked up and saw the cheese. “Mmm,” he thought. “I want that cheese. But how can I get it?”\n\nHe had an idea. He smiled and said, “Good morning, beautiful crow! You look so lovely today! Your feathers are shiny and black.”\n\nThe crow was surprised, but she felt proud.\n\n“I heard that you have the sweetest voice in the forest,” said the fox. “Could you sing a song for me?”\n\nThe crow was very happy. “Of course!” she thought. She opened her mouth to sing, “Caw! Caw!”\n\nThe cheese fell down. The fox caught it quickly. “Thank you!” he said, and he ran away laughing.\n\nThe crow sat alone on the branch. “I was foolish,” she said sadly. “I listened to flattery.”\n\nMoral: Be careful of people who say too many sweet words.","tr":null,"gl":{"a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","crow":"qarg'a","found":"topdi","big":"katta","piece":"bo'lak","of":"-ning; -dan","cheese":"pishloq","she":"u (ayol)","was":"edi","very":"juda","happy":"xursand, baxtli","flew":"uchdi","up":"yuqoriga","to":"-ga; uchun","high":"baland","branch":"shox","tree":"daraxt","and":"va","sat":"o'tirdi","there":"u yerda; bor","wanted":"xohladi","eat":"yemoq","her":"uni; uning (ayol)","in":"ichida, -da","peace":"tinchlik, xotirjamlik","hungry":"och","fox":"tulki","walked":"yurdi","past":"o'tmish; yonidan","he":"u (erkak)","looked":"qaradi","saw":"ko'rdi","the":"(aniq artikl)","mmm":"mmm (zavq)","thought":"o'yladi; fikr","i":"men","want":"xohlamoq","that":"u, o'sha; -ki","but":"lekin, ammo","how":"qanday","can":"qila olmoq","get":"olmoq, bo'lmoq","it":"u (narsa)","had":"bor edi; -gan edi","an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","idea":"g'oya","smiled":"jilmaydi","said":"dedi","good":"yaxshi","morning":"ertalab, tong","beautiful":"chiroyli","you":"sen, siz","look":"qaramoq","so":"shuning uchun; shunday","lovely":"yoqimli","today":"bugun",